{"id": "EUVD-2026-101396", "enisaUuid": "3e96d858-abef-3be0-9d9a-e16565746a85", "description": "A Stack-based Buffer Overflow vulnerability in the routing protocol daemon (rpd) of Juniper Networks Junos OS and Junos OS Evolved allows an attacker with access to a configured BGP peering session to cause a denial of service by sending a crafted BGP route attribute, which is processed while a BGP RIB streaming telemetry subscription is active.\n\nThis issue does not affect Junos OS versions prior to 22.1R1.\nThis issue does not affect Junos OS Evolved versions prior to 22.1R1-EVO.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T16:57:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T19:05:07", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L/AU:Y/R:A/V:C/RE:M", "references": ["https://supportportal.juniper.net/JSA112187"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102180", "GHSA-wwmf-2ph2-pvvc"], "assigner": "juniper", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "122dad6c-60cd-36ee-a6da-deb19b962b81", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "25.4 <25.4R1-S3"}, {"id": "221b60a6-45aa-3b97-961f-2c035591810c", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "24.2 <24.2R2-S5.5"}, {"id": "3f4d77d1-7832-3fea-acb6-61df123b6fd3", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "24.2 <24.2R2-S5.6-EVO"}, {"id": "5810df08-f599-3697-9dab-0798c6a272f7", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "25.2 <25.2R2-S2-EVO"}, {"id": "5834f87c-6d8d-3c12-93ad-a2cd814773d9", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "25.4 <25.4R1-S3-EVO"}, {"id": "62cbe008-1228-32aa-81e2-31eba3fb7d30", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "0 <23.2R2-S7.7"}, {"id": "631c847c-367